{
  "rebuttals": [
    {
      "ruling_id": "move2-integrated-customer-competition",
      "stance": "challenge",
      "argument": "The ruling assumes that Dunkin's $1.50 discount on the breakfast Meal Deal in 15 stores with local marketing and opt-in/stop rules will be effective and economically viable without sufficiently accounting for the full-price purchases that would have occurred anyway, risking unprofitable traffic. The dossier facts d.dunkin.k6 and d.dunkin.k7 explicitly caution that redemption alone is not profit and that full accounting of discount costs and repeat visit economics is necessary. Therefore, the causal link that Dunkin's discount and marketing efforts will reliably improve competitive position without risking economic harm is not fully supported.",
      "link": "dunkin_meal_deal",
      "cite": ["d.dunkin.k6", "d.dunkin.k7"]
    }
  ]
}
// I challenge the causal link that Dunkin's $1.50 discount and local marketing in 15 stores will be beneficial without risking unprofitable traffic, citing the dossier constraints on discount economics and the need for monitoring store-level economics.

